# Bytecode from the ci/ checkers. They are plain scripts, not a package;
# nothing imports them except their own self-tests.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated by build.sh. cosim-closure.tar, mixsim-closure.tar,
# viewer-closure.tar, vams-closure.tar and host-closure.tar are the engines',
# the viewers' and the die build's tools' closures packed from the host's Nix
# store (nix/cosim-closure.txt, nix/mixsim-closure.txt, nix/viewer-closure.txt,
# nix/vams-closure.txt, nix/host-closure.txt), and the build context must
# carry them, so .dockerignore does not list them.
manifest.json
cosim-closure.tar
cosim-closure.tar.tmp
mixsim-closure.tar
mixsim-closure.tar.tmp
viewer-closure.tar
viewer-closure.tar.tmp
vams-closure.tar
vams-closure.tar.tmp
host-closure.tar
host-closure.tar.tmp
tool-identity.facts.json
# The LibreLane launcher build.sh writes with nix/build-env.sh, for the
# runtime stage to copy.
librelane-launcher
librelane-launcher.tmp

*.log

# Local session-continuity tracking (not part of the project)
SESSION_LOG.md

# Sibling sources staged into the build context by stage-sources.sh. Fetched
# shallow at the pinned sha, never copied from a working tree; every tree here
# is reproducible from staging.pin, so none of it belongs in git.
staging/

# Die views staged into the build context by stage-die-views.sh, from the
# directory STAGE_DIE_VIEWS_DIR names; die-views.sha256 pins every byte.
die-views/

# Nix: `nix build` writes ./result; direnv writes .direnv/
result
result-*
.direnv/

# OpenROAD sidecar working state: the managed upstream checkout (~3 GB) and
# the host virtualenv the live gate runs in. Both are rebuildable from
# openroad/openroad.pin.
openroad/.openroad-src/
openroad/.venv/

# Demo / project artifacts under examples/<project>/. The export and the verify
# stage regenerate everything below; only the heavy and scratch files are
# ignored. The light deliverables are tracked on purpose (a fresh clone then
# opens the demo in chiplet-studio and carries the DRC results without a
# rebuild): the .chiplet + MANIFEST.md at the outputs/ root, the _interposer.gds
# and *.json sidecars under outputs/layout/, and the reports under
# outputs/reports/.
#
# Keep this block in lockstep with .dockerignore, and with the per-project
# .gitignore that `adk-new-project` scaffolds (same patterns, project-relative).
#
# outputs/ : the GDS layouts and their sidecars live under layout/; ignore only
#            the heavy layout/*_complete.gds, the intermediate .hyp, the DRC
#            working dir and the run logs. The DRC reports
#            (reports/*_assembly_drc.lyrdb, reports/*_cupillar_drc.json) and
#            MANIFEST.md stay tracked.
examples/**/outputs/layout/*_complete.gds
examples/**/outputs/*.hyp
examples/**/outputs/reports/assembly_drc/
examples/**/outputs/logs/
# kicad/ : KiCad's own scratch (caches, autosaves, lock files, local prefs).
examples/**/*-backups/
examples/**/fp-info-cache
examples/**/*.kicad_prl
examples/**/_autosave-*
examples/**/*.lck
